# A darray whose storage OUTLIVES the function (a parameter) grown while a by-value LOCAL
# arena is the ambient allocator: the new backing buffer lives in `arena`, which is freed on
# return -- a use-after-free. stage0:
#   darray push grows a non-local darray from local arena "arena"; its backing buffer is freed when "arena" goes out of scope (use-after-free). ...
# (plus the carrier-type warning on the `Arena` local; `in <arena>:` is a deprecated surface,
# and this fixture pins that the check still guards it.)
#
# stage1 fired for `arena: Arena = zeroed` but NOT for `mutable Arena`: its by-value-local
# collector tested the bare identifier, and `mutable` wrapped it. Measured on stage0: bare
# and `mutable` both fire, `lmut` does not, an `Arena&` parameter does not.
def grow_param_from_local_arena(out: mutable darray[i64]&) -> void can[Memory.Allocate, Abort.Panic]:
    arena: mutable Arena = zeroed
    in arena:
        out.push(1)
